====Noun====
{{en-noun|+|*<l:now,UK,_,colloquial>}}

# {{senseid|en|Q577}} A period of time akin to the time taken for the [[Earth]] to [[undergo]] a full [[cycle]] of seasons.
#: {{alti|en|y<id:Q577>|yr<id:Q577><qq:symbols>}}
#: {{syn|en|annum<id:Q577>|mul:a<id:Q577>}}
#: {{ux|en|We moved to this town a '''year''' ago.}}
#: {{ux|en|I quit smoking exactly one '''year''' ago.}}
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|book=Luke|chapter=2|verses=41–42|folio=lxvj|passage=And his father and mother went to hieruſalem every '''yeare''' att the feeſte of eſter. And when he was xij. '''yere''' olde&nbsp;/ they went vppe to hieruſalem after the cuſtome of the feeſte&nbsp;/ {{...}}|norm=And his father and mother went to Jerusalem every '''year''' at the feast of Easter. And when he was 7 '''year''' old, they went up to Jerusalem after the custom of the feast,{{nb...}}}}
## {{senseid|en|Q189607}} The time taken for the [[Earth]] to return to the same position along the [[ecliptic]], completing a full cycle of [[season]]s; a [[tropical year]] or [[solar year]].
## {{senseid|en|Q2281928}} The time taken for the Earth to orbit the [[Sun]] with respect to the [[fixed stars]]; a [[sidereal year]].
## {{senseid|en|Q10593422}} The length of twelve [[lunation|lunations]]; the time taken for any moon [[phase]] to happen twelve times; a [[lunar year]].
## {{senseid|en|Q3186692}} The length of a year as marked by a calendar, 365 or 366 days in the [[Gregorian calendar]]; a [[calendar year]].
## {{senseid|en|Q217208}} The [[mean]] length of a calendar year in the [[Julian calendar]], that is, 365.25 [[solar day|solar days]]; a [[Julian year]].
# {{senseid|en|Q37640}} {{lb|en|by extension}} An [[orbital#Adjective|orbital]] [[period#Noun|period]]: the period of one revolution in any particular [[orbit#Noun|orbit]]: The time it takes for any astronomical object (such as a [[planet]], [[dwarf planet]], [[small Solar System body]], or [[comet]]) in direct orbit around a [[star]] (such as the [[Sun]]) to make one revolution around the star.
#: {{ux|en|Mars goes around the sun once in a Martian '''year''', or 1.88 Earth years.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|system=PC|scene=Citdael|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|passage=Shepard: What can you tell me about the Citadel Council?<br>Avina: Originally, the Council consisted of representatives from the asari and salarians, the two dominant species in Citadel space.<br>Roughly 1,304 galactic standard '''years''' ago, turians were invited to join the Council in recognition of the role they played during the Krogan Rebellion.}}
# A [[period]] between set [[date]]s that mark a year, such as from January 1 to December 31 by the [[Gregorian calendar]], from Tishri 1 to Elul 29 by the [[Jewish calendar]], and from Muharram 1 to Dhu al-Hijjah 29 or 30 by the [[Islamic calendar]].
#: {{ux|en|A normal '''year''' has 365 full days, but there are 366 days in a leap '''year'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was born in the '''year''' 1950.}}
#: {{ux|en|This Chinese '''year''' is the '''year''' of the Ox.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-07-20|volume=408|issue=8845
|url=https://www.economist.com/business/2013/07/20/the-attack-of-the-moocs|title=The attack of the MOOCs
|passage=Dotcom mania was slow in coming to higher education, but now it has the venerable industry firmly in its grip. Since the launch early last '''year''' of Udacity and Coursera, two Silicon Valley start-ups offering free education through MOOCs, massive open online courses, the ivory towers of academia have been shaken to their foundations.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200717183119/https://www.economist.com/business/2013/07/20/the-attack-of-the-moocs}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Oscar Holland|title=Construction of world’s tallest abandoned skyscraper to resume after a decade|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/24/style/china-goldin-finance-117-construction-resumes-hnk-intl|date=2025-04-24|passage=Construction of the world’s tallest unoccupied skyscraper may resume as early as next week, almost 10 '''years''' after work ground to a halt, according to Chinese state media.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260322222838/https://www.cnn.com/2025/04/24/style/china-goldin-finance-117-construction-resumes-hnk-intl|archivedate=22 March 2026}}
# A scheduled part of a [[calendar year]] spent in a specific [[activity]].
#: {{ux|en|During this school '''year''' I have to get up at 6:30 to catch the bus.}}
## A [[level]] or [[grade]] in [[school]] or [[college]].
##: {{ux|en|Every second-'''year''' student must select an area of specialization.}}
##: {{ux|en|The exams in '''year''' 12 at high school are the most difficult.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'm the oldest student in my '''year''' because I've repeated twice.}}
# The proportion of a creature's [[lifespan]] equivalent to one year of an average human lifespan (see also [[dog year]]).
#: {{ux|en|Geneticists have created baker's yeast that can live to 800 in yeast '''years'''.}}

